 "title": "Each eigenvalue's eigenvectors on the cut-open torus are one polynomial",
 "subject": "Networks of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "At sides 2^m the eigenvectors of the cut-open torus at each eigenvalue are one polynomial G times polynomials in Y = k\u00b2 + k, proved from a self-adjointness and a shared shift ratio, so their number is set by deg G alone. deg G matches the Kloosterman count at every eigenvalue to side 512 (computed); bounding it, and the Jordan chains the collapse needs, stay open.",
